  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are the sides that are opposite the ${45}^{∘}$ angles. So in the given triangle, the legs have length $4.$\n\nConsequently, the hypotenuse has a length of\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
